<title>SOUTH AFRICA: HL&amp;H narrows half yr loss, no div.</title>
<headline>HL&amp;H narrows half yr loss, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Loss per shr (cts)    7.8	   vs  26.7  loss</p>
<p>    Attrib loss	    11.73	  vs  40.01 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	 58.21	  vs  12.58 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.31	  vs   4.53</p>
<p>    Net financing costs  37.35	  vs  58.04</p>
<p>Share of associated</p>
<p>     companies losses    69.63	  vs  22.90 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		659.81	  vs 767.36</p>
<p>Full name: Hunt Leuchars &amp; Hepburn Holdings Ltd (food)</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     38.33	 vs   -</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that in view of the results for the past six months, no interim dividend would be declared.</p>
<p>HL&amp;H said that due to the significant effect of Rainbow Chicken Ltd's results it expected that the group would report a loss for the full year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
